  "id": "COMPOUND:3232 - PROTEIN:2270",
  "verbalization": "SU9516 is implicated in the inhibition of mRNA interferase EndoA through a series of molecular interactions involving the V-type sodium ATPase subunit K. This subunit is a target of multiple compounds, including Alsterpaullone, Indirubin-3'-monoxime, and [(2E,6E)-1-Oxo-8-hydroxy-2,6-dimethylocta-2,6-dien-1-yl]beta-D-glucopyranoside, all of which are known to interact with the V-type sodium ATPase. The evidence suggests that SU9516 may act as a modulator of this enzyme, potentially through a mechanism that involves the inhibition of the V-type sodium ATPase subunit K, which in turn affects the activity of mRNA interferase EndoA. The cumulative scores from the three paths indicate a plausible, though not definitive, relationship between SU9516 and EndoA, supported by the shared target of the V-type sodium ATPase subunit K. The mechanism appears to involve a pathway where the inhibition of the ATPase subunit K leads to a downstream effect on EndoA, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
